extends layout

block content
  .col-md-12.cardSpacer
    #page-header-container(style='align-items:flex-start')
      #page-title-container
        h3#page-title About SumExplorer
        .sub-page-header.text-muted Independent Sumcoin blockchain data, transaction lookup, and network visibility.
      .cardSpacer.clearfix

    .card.card-default.border-0.cardSpacer
      .card-header
        strong SumExplorer at a glance
      .card-body
        p.lead.mb-3 SumExplorer is a public Sumcoin blockchain explorer built to help users verify transactions, inspect blocks, review public address activity, and monitor the Sumcoin network.
        p.mb-0 The explorer does not hold coins, operate as an exchange, or control wallet balances. It reads public blockchain data and presents it in a searchable format so users can independently confirm what has happened on-chain.

    .row
      .col-md-6.cardSpacer
        .card.card-default.border-0.h-100
          .card-header
            strong What the explorer shows
          .card-body
            ul.mb-0
              li Recent Sumcoin blocks and transactions.
              li Transaction IDs, confirmations, timestamps, and public outputs.
              li Public address balances and address transaction history.
              li Rich list information and visible coin distribution.
              li Network information such as peers, block height, difficulty, and hashrate.
      .col-md-6.cardSpacer
        .card.card-default.border-0.h-100
          .card-header
            strong What the explorer cannot do
          .card-body
            ul.mb-0
              li It cannot reverse, cancel, or accelerate a transaction.
              li It cannot recover private keys, seed words, or wallet passwords.
              li It cannot identify the owner of a public blockchain address.
              li It cannot move funds or change blockchain history.
              li It cannot replace a wallet, node, exchange, or backup.

    .card.card-default.border-0.cardSpacer
      .card-header
        strong Why blockchain explorers matter
      .card-body
        p Blockchain explorers give users a public way to check whether a transaction was broadcast, included in a block, and confirmed by the network. This is useful when comparing wallet status, exchange deposits, payments, and public address balances.
        p.mb-0 SumExplorer is intended to make Sumcoin activity easier to review without requiring every visitor to run a full node or inspect raw blockchain data manually.
